1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,563
This is ProofBox, a containment-first control plane for AI agents.

2
00:00:05,563 --> 00:00:08,721
Built for Vultr Agent Rush, challenge one:

3
00:00:08,721 --> 00:00:10,075
Blast Radius Zero.

4
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:14,454
Agents now run code and drive browsers.

5
00:00:14,454 --> 00:00:21,941
One bad step can read your API keys, hit the cloud metadata endpoint, or submit a form you never approved.

6
00:00:21,941 --> 00:00:25,825
You need to contain every step, and prove that you did.

7
00:00:27,433 --> 00:00:31,493
ProofBox puts a control plane between the model and the machine.

8
00:00:31,493 --> 00:00:38,977
The server validates every plan, adds its own containment probes, and puts a human gate on anything with side effects.

9
00:00:38,977 --> 00:00:45,383
Each step runs in a fresh sandbox that is destroyed afterwards, and comes back with a signed receipt.

10
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,743
One note before the demo.

11
00:00:48,743 --> 00:00:50,765
This build runs in mock mode.

12
00:00:50,765 --> 00:00:55,157
The sandbox is simulated, and the app says so on every receipt.

13
00:00:55,157 --> 00:00:59,200
The policy rules and the receipt signatures are real code.

14
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:01,951
Prove-It Python.

15
00:01:01,951 --> 00:01:02,670
The claim:

16
00:01:02,670 --> 00:01:07,128
the sum of primes below one hundred is one thousand and sixty.

17
00:01:07,128 --> 00:01:15,255
The planner writes the step, the server dispatches it, and the receipt comes back hashed and signed with Ed25519.

18
00:01:15,255 --> 00:01:18,275
I can verify it right here in the browser.

19
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:21,491
Now the containment moment.

20
00:01:21,491 --> 00:01:24,410
The server, not the model, added this probe.

21
00:01:24,410 --> 00:01:29,916
It tries to read the API key, the host disk, cloud metadata, and the Docker socket.

22
00:01:29,916 --> 00:01:32,968
All blocked, and the secret shows up redacted.

23
00:01:32,968 --> 00:01:36,550
A two gigabyte allocation is killed at the memory cap.

24
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:38,876
CSV Analyst.

25
00:01:38,876 --> 00:01:46,250
The agent guesses the wrong column, sees the key error, fixes it, and retries in a brand new sandbox.

26
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:51,725
Trying to post the data to an outside host is blocked by the egress policy.

27
00:01:53,133 --> 00:01:54,638
Research with Receipts.

28
00:01:54,638 --> 00:01:59,805
The browser may only reach hosts I typed that are also on the server allowlist.

29
00:01:59,805 --> 00:02:03,533
Before the form is submitted, ProofBox stops and asks me.

30
00:02:03,533 --> 00:02:05,757
I deny, and the submit never runs.

31
00:02:05,757 --> 00:02:10,008
I run it again and approve, and the receipt records the decision.

32
00:02:10,933 --> 00:02:12,217
What is real today:

33
00:02:12,217 --> 00:02:21,878
plan validation, server-inserted probes, the human gate, the egress allowlist, secret redaction, and signed receipts anyone can verify offline.

34
00:02:21,878 --> 00:02:22,959
What comes next:

35
00:02:22,959 --> 00:02:29,783
Vultr Serverless Inference for the model calls, and Docker with gVisor on a Vultr VM for the sandbox.

36
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,139
ProofBox.

37
00:02:32,139 --> 00:02:34,850
Blast radius zero, with receipts.

